@startuml
title kubescape/host-scanner - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

' External entities
rectangle "HTTP Client" as Client
rectangle "Operator" as Operator
rectangle "E2E Test Suite (Go)\nProvider-specific selection via\n//go:build <provider>" as Tests

cloud "Kubernetes Cluster" as K8s {
  node "Worker Node" as Node {
    node "Host Filesystem\n(/etc, /run, /var/lib)" as FS
    component "kubelet" as Kubelet
    component "Container Runtime\n(containerd / CRI-O)" as Runtime

    node "Pod: host-scanner (DaemonSet)\n[privileged]" as Pod {
      component "host-scanner Service" as Service
      component "HTTP API" as HTTP
      component "Host Info Collector" as Collector
      component "CNI Resolver" as CNI
      component "JSON Sanitizer" as Sanitizer
    }
  }
}

file "Control-plane JSON Input" as JsonIn
file "Sanitized JSON Output" as JsonOut

' Deployments and operational context
Operator --> K8s : Deploy privileged DaemonSet\n(C-004)
Client --> HTTP : HTTP requests (GET)\nUnknown path -> 404\n(FR-001, NFR-003)

' Internal interactions
Collector --> FS : Read host info\n(DR-003)
Collector --> CNI : Request resolved CNI dir\n(DR-004)
CNI --> Kubelet : Read runtime type/defaults/config\n(FR-002)
CNI --> Runtime : Inspect runtime configuration\n(FR-002)
CNI --> FS : Read config files and CLI args\nResolve to /etc/cni/ | /var/lib/cni/ | subpaths\n(FR-002, DR-003, DR-004)

Sanitizer --> JsonIn : Accept JSON with\nprovider config secrets\n(FR-003, DR-005)
Sanitizer --> JsonOut : Output sanitized JSON\n(secrets removed)\n(FR-003, NFR-001, DR-006)

' Test interactions and verification
Tests --> HTTP : E2E HTTP checks\n404 for /doesnotexist\n(FR-001, NFR-003)
Tests --> CNI : Verify directory resolution across\nprovider/runtime scenarios\n(FR-002, DR-003, DR-004)
Tests --> Sanitizer : Verify secret removal and\nstructure preservation\n(FR-003, NFR-001, DR-006)
note right of Tests
  Provider-specific expected data selection
  via Go build tags:
  //go:build <provider>
  (NFR-002, C-001, DR-007)
end note

' Containment and associations
Pod -[hidden]down- Service
Service -[hidden]down- HTTP
Service -[hidden]down- Collector
Service -[hidden]down- CNI
Service -[hidden]down- Sanitizer

' Notes for clarity
note right of HTTP
  HTTP API uses standard request/response semantics
  and returns 404 for unknown paths like /doesnotexist.
  (FR-001, NFR-003, DR-001, DR-002)
end note

note bottom of CNI
  Resolves CNI configuration directory:
  - Defaults: /etc/cni/ (kubelet/containerd)
  - Explicit CLI arg: /var/lib/cni/
  - Config-derived: specific CNI subpaths
  (FR-002)
end note

note right of Sanitizer
  Removes encryption provider configuration secrets
  from control-plane JSON before output.
  (FR-003, NFR-001)
end note

@enduml
